updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: claim-boundedness
axis_gloss: "whether a claim states the limits of what it covers, or is asserted without any declared boundary"
poles:
  a: bounded-claim
  b: unbounded-claim
split: lone-exception
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 12
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(25) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On claim boundedness — whether a claim states the limits of what it covers, or
  is asserted without any declared boundary — the records assert both bounded
  claim (24 judgments, 16 authored) and unbounded claim (1 judgments, 0
  authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    24 judgments sit at bounded-claim (16 authored) and 1 at unbounded-claim (0
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    The full proposal.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      bounded claim becomes the stated rule across its scope.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      - "J0008"
      - "J0138"
      - "J0150"
      - "J0154"
      - "J0167"
      - "J0168"
  - name: B
    description: >
      unbounded claim becomes the stated rule across its scope.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      - "J0728"
  - name: C
    description: >
      One pole is the rule; the other is a written carve-out for a named case.
    cost: "not yet drafted"
    risk: "not yet drafted"
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "not yet drafted"
    evidence_for:
      []

